define.h

_ntrac_ : 1 (qv), 2(qv+o3)
     for new variable : 1) ntrac = 3
                        2) initialize  : o3suv.F, seto3p.F
                        3) physics     : o3phys.F

_ncldg_ : 0 (no-prognostic cld), 1 (qc:cloud water only),
          2 ( qci, qrs), 4 (qc,qi,qr,qs)

          *** automatically tell cloud inptu at initial input

ICE : saturation vapor pressure w.r.t. ice
INTERACTIVE_STRATUS : define cloudiness w.r.t. qci, qrs....

    currently : cf = function (RH, qci), Randall's formula
    ==> produces less clouds

    -- major tuning place for cloudiness computation
    -- cf can be a function of (RH, qci, z, lat ...) Moorthi
        
ICECLOUD :
    optical properties depending upon qci
    8-bands uv+vis 
    same as in Moorthi & Yu-tai, but was modified 
        Moorthis code came from Yu-tai, but single column and some 
        changes
    code is different but method is same except for old aerosol, and 
          swflux is the old one. old aerosol with ibnd=2 is fine.
        Moorthi and Yu-tai merged with cvs GSM radiation, but with
        option  for old radiation

minor : all radiation tuning parameters are in gradini
           (ibnd, icfc, icwp..iswsrc)

another tuning in cloud2 is RHcrit in gscond.F
    u00b, u00t : 85 % for condensation

2005-01-01 (ECPC)

changes to cvs noah version

1.  Generalized cnvrt and chgdates.  These programs are now combined into
    one program in libs/etc/utils/scnvrt.F.  The program is independent
    of model resolution, and of gsm or rsm (specified by data card).  The
    scripts, chgdates, rchgdates, cnvrt, rcnvrt, ... are now consolidated
    into scnvrt.

2.  Complete clean-up of surface program.

        2.1  sfcl library now does surface file merging.  the program became a
         subroutine (sfc) and is called by forecast program as well as by
         sfc0 program.
    2.2  sfc0 program is introduced.  This program reads any type of sfc
         file, converts to the sfc file type of the program you are
         about to run.  Some fields are calculated from available
         fields, while others are filled by grib files.
    2.3  The specification of sfc file structure is now done at two
         places.  One in the libs/lib/modelib/sfcfld.F, and the other in
         the srcs/src/include files, varsfc.h, comsfc.h and comsfcmrg.h
    2.4  The specification of surface grib files to be read in by subroutine
         sfc and program sfc0 is specified in srcs/src/inlucde/vargrb.h
    2.5  fixio routine is rewritten.  It does not require any changes even
         surface file structure is changed.  It also became common to gsm
         and rsm.  The common is rearranged to make this possible.  This
         introduced comsfc.h and comsfcmrg.h
    2.6  sfc file structure is now same for gsm and rsm. mountain variance
         in rsm sfc file is removed.  It is now read in separately.

3.  Unification of key gsm and rsm prgrams.  In order to make the change in
    physics transparent between gsm and rsm, the following programs are now
    merged into one.

        gbphys and rbphys   ......  physics driver routines
    grphys and rrphys   ......  basic radiation driver routine
    grrad1 and rgrrad1  ......  second level radiation driver routine 1
    grrad2 and rgrrad2  ......  second level radiation driver routine 2
    gradpre and rradpre ......  radiation initialization routine 1
    gradini and rradini ......  radiation initialization routine 2
        fixio and rfixio    ......  sfc file i/o (as noted in 2. above)

        As a result of these unifications, osu and noah land surface packages
        are running both on gsm and rsm.

4.  Continuous integration

        Because of the change of sfc program into subroutine, the forecast
    programs (gsm and rsm) can be integrated without interraption.  The
    i/o of rsm is modified (gsm was already modified) to generate
    history files in speficied intervals during continuous integrations
    (without specifying the file name in the script).  The base field i/o
    for rsm is also modified to read files during the integration.

5.  Various clean-ups.

        5.1  Many of the unused routines are removed.
        5.2  Only used physics packages are compiled.
        5.3  Binary albedo related file reads are removed and replaced
         with grib file reads.  This eliminated cnvalb, cnvaer and
         albaer programs (and directories).
    5.4  rbln and rloc programs are removed (they are not used).
        5.5  mtn program is removed from rsm runs.
        5.6  use of more consistent variable names in configure and run
         scripts.

The results of the integration will change due to various reasons.
        1.  Quality control in sfc subroutine is much looser.
        2.  Spatial interpolation is improved.
        3.  Use of grib albedo/aerosol vs. binary files cause differences.
        4.  A couple of very minor errors are found and fixed.
          4.1 verifying dates in fixrd was one day off
          4.2 undefined variables in rradini

grims physcis versions, 2011-04-10

v1.0 : ra2 physics 
v2.0 : ncep seasonal forecast physcis
v3.0 : nml physcis
	v.3.1 : v.3.0 + UV_CMT in SAS + HYBRID vertical coordinate
	v.3.2 : v.3.1 + Han and Pan GFS shallow and deep convections
	v.3.3 : v.3.2 + w1-w4 reformulations in sas, and thermal excess in ysu
v4.0 : ncep gfs physics as of jan 2011
v5.0 : ncar-wrf unified physics
